# Models

Concrete models subclass an abstract `BaseModel` with indexed `created_at` (`default=timezone.now`) and `updated_at` (`auto_now=True`). Prefer `Meta.constraints` for rules the database can enforce. Use `clean` only for simple checks on non-relational fields. Properties and methods stay simple and non-relational. Anything that spans relations or does real work is a service or selector.

```python
# ❌ BAD — a uniqueness rule and a relation query inside clean
def clean(self):
    if User.objects.filter(email=self.email).exclude(pk=self.pk).exists():
        raise ValidationError({"email": "taken"})

# ✅ GOOD
class BaseModel(models.Model):
    created_at = models.DateTimeField(db_index=True, default=timezone.now)
    updated_at = models.DateTimeField(auto_now=True)

    class Meta:
        abstract = True


class User(BaseModel):
    email = models.EmailField()

    class Meta:
        constraints = [
            models.UniqueConstraint(fields=["email"], name="unique_user_email"),
        ]

    def clean(self):
        if self.email != self.email.lower():
            raise ValidationError({"email": "must be lowercase"})
```
